  "verificationBoundary": [
    "Frozen candidate matched 173 tracked and owned child/client source inputs after LF normalization. Pending guardian, V24 classification and reporting changes excluded.",
    "Foreground initialization/reentry/connection refreshes facts only. New create/cancel uses fresh secure random key; retry uses original durable input/key/version and prior committed expiry-recovery protocol. Child cannot approve, edit policies or grant operating-system access.",
    "Tests cover response-loss recovery, refusal to discard UNKNOWN, authorization hiding, factory/lifecycle races, late response suppression, pagination, strong cancellation, confirmation, 320px/1.5 text scaling, actual Enter/directional/select activation, and merged actionable application semantics.",
    "Browser renders actual session/journal/widgets in installed Chrome at 390x844 and 1280x900. Explicit public fixture entry uses in-memory identity/service data, no production connection/storage. Real keyboard text must appear in confirmation; create/cancel/unknown/offline and production Web boundary verified. Screenshots use application viewport rather than full DOM bounds.",
    "Synthetic service fixture preserves original accepted reason/time/version; the observed optional-reason mismatch was fixed in the fixture rather than relaxing production journal consistency checks.",
    "Builds prove compilation and packaging. Android debug APK uses the normal main entry with no deployment URL embedded; it has not been installed or exercised for the new request workflow in this stage. Web production enrollment remains disabled.",
    "No backend source/migration changed or new backend/MySQL/OceanBase tests run in this stage; original real HTTP/MySQL recovery evidence remains in stage-submission-recovery-verification.json. Do not combine separate fixtures into a production native end-to-end claim.",
    "Actual Android process recovery, real Spring product-session/UI journey, television vendor/IME compatibility, background reliability, EMM and operating-system enforcement remain required. No production server deployment in this stage.",
    "Owned local preview servers were stopped after acceptance; parallel task services and working changes preserved."
